;; LE-18: a vector against a scalar is a diagnosed type error, not a SIGSEGV.
;;
;; Element-wise arithmetic dispatched on the LEFT operand alone, so a Scheme
;; vector on the left sent the pair to the Scheme-vector kernel, which read the
;; scalar 2 as `[len:i64][tagged elems...]` and loaded its first element at
;; 2 + 8:
;;
;;   before   [Eshkol] fatal signal: SIGSEGV at address 0x…0a, exit 139,
;;            no diagnostic, no source location, uncatchable
;;   after    input.esk:14:14: Type error in tensor-mul: expected tensor,
;;            got integer, exit 1
(display "before")
(newline)
(display (* (vector 1 2) 2))
(display "MUST-NOT-PRINT")
(newline)
